1.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['My family felt so complete': Usha Vance on why she hesitated before having fourth child ]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132941653.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/usha-vance-thought-fourth-child-would-disrupt-family-dynamic-says-its-only-become-happier/articleshow/132941653.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/usha-vance-thought-fourth-child-would-disrupt-family-dynamic-says-its-only-become-happier/articleshow/132941653.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-05T20:37:36+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132941653,imgsize-59445.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[An 11-year-old autistic boy wanted to trick-or-treat in summer; neighbors opened their doors and...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132934009.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A heartfelt Facebook post from a mother seeking birthday cheer for her autistic son ignited an incredible wave of community support. Eighty-three families joined in a unique summer trick-or-treat celebration for Soren, showering him with handcrafted gifts and candies. This touching event not only spread joy but also shed light on the importance of acceptance, dismantling stereotypes associated with autism and showcasing the strength of community bonds.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-11-year-old-autistic-boy-wanted-to-trick-or-treat-in-summer-83-neighbors-opened-their-doors-and-turned-his-birthday-into-halloween/articleshow/132934009.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-11-year-old-autistic-boy-wanted-to-trick-or-treat-in-summer-83-neighbors-opened-their-doors-and-turned-his-birthday-into-halloween/articleshow/132934009.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-05T20:30:36+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132940759,imgsize-1379205.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet Seungah Chung, the US eighth-grader who used 200 ants to discover landmark navigation]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132925886.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A bright young student embarked on a fascinating ant navigation experiment fueled by her natural curiosity. Through her meticulous research, she uncovered that ants primarily depend on visual markers for navigation. This groundbreaking project garnered her acclaim at a well-regarded science competition, showcasing the potential of such findings to inspire the development of innovative robots and autonomous systems.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/meet-seungah-chung-the-us-eighth-grader-who-used-200-ants-and-a-maze-to-discover-they-navigate-by-landmarks/articleshow/132925886.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/meet-seungah-chung-the-us-eighth-grader-who-used-200-ants-and-a-maze-to-discover-they-navigate-by-landmarks/articleshow/132925886.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-05T17:54:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132926515,imgsize-123181.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Over 3,000 cases of deadly fungus Candida auris reported in US: What it is, how it spreads- explained]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin