streets-but-scientists-say-the-biggest-impact-could-be-on-air-conditioning-bills/articleshow/132902597.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/singapore-is-planting-one-million-trees-to-cool-its-streets-but-scientists-say-the-biggest-impact-could-be-on-air-conditioning-bills/articleshow/132902597.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-05T15:06:59+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132902597,imgsize-361198.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Stacy Brooks expected to dislike downtown Minneapolis, but a one-year trial changed her mind]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132925921.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Stacy Brooks, originally from northern Minnesota, discovered a newfound happiness in her urban high-rise. After a year-long experiment, she and her husband are in the process of purchasing their 19th-floor apartment. Their daily routine transformed into leisurely walks, indulging in community amenities, and savoring a variety of local dining options. The supportive community of childfree neighbors further enhanced her experience, marking a significant departure from her previous suburban life.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/stacy-brooks-expected-to-dislike-downtown-minneapolis-but-a-one-year-trial-changed-her-mind-she-and-her-husband-are-now-negotiating-to-buy-their-condo/articleshow/132925921.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/stacy-brooks-expected-to-dislike-downtown-minneapolis-but-a-one-year-trial-changed-her-mind-she-and-her-husband-are-now-negotiating-to-buy-their-condo/articleshow/132925921.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-05T19:08:57+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132932762,imgsize-1129801.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Trump's immigration crackdown hits US military families; over 50 spouses, parents detained]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132919173.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Dozens of parents and spouses of US service members face detention and deportation. This marks a significant shift from prior bipartisan immigration policies for military families. Many are detained during routine immigration status adjustment appointments. The Department of Homeland Security states military service does not exempt violations of immigration laws. These detentions negatively impact military readiness and family stability.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/donald-trumps-immigration-crackdown-hits-us-military-families-over-50-spouses-parents-detained/articleshow/132919173.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/donald-trumps-immigration-crackdown-hits-us-military-families-over-50-spouses-parents-detained/articleshow/132919173.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-05T17:41:35+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132925769,imgsize-744489.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Texas uses discarded Christmas trees to help sea turtles survive]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132925196.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Discarded Christmas trees are repurposed to build sand dunes along the Texas coast.  These trees are placed on beaches to trap shifting sand and strengthen the shoreline.  This process occurs before the sea turtle nesting season begins each year.  The new dunes provide a protective barrier for relocated sea turtle eggs.  This initiative helps ensure a safer environment for hatchlings during their development.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/texas-has-been-using-discarded-christmas-trees-on-its-beaches-for-years-and-theyre-quietly-helping-sea-turtles-survive/articleshow/132925196.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/texas-has-been-using-discarded-christmas-trees-on-its-beaches-for-years-and-theyre-quietly-helping-sea-turtles-survive/articleshow/132925196.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-05T17:46:34+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132925196,imgsize-244202.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[California will close the westbound Zampa Bridge for 53 hours to replace part of its deck]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132921898.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Important notice for travelers: Westbound access on the Al Zampa Memorial Bridge will be entirely shut down for 53 hours, commencing on Friday, August 21, and concluding on Monday, August 24, to facilitate necessary repairs. Motorists are urged to anticipate heavy delays and to follow detour signs. Please be advised that foot and bicycle traffic will also be halted during this repair window. Prepare your travel plans accordingly.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/california-will-close-the-westbound-zampa-bridge-for-53-hours-to-replace-part-of-its-deck-creating-a-major-weekend-detour-between-vallejo-and-the-east-bay/articleshow/132921898.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/california-will-close-the-westbound-zampa-bridge-for-53-hours-to-replace-part-of-its-deck-creating-a-major-weekend-detour-between-vallejo-and-the-east-bay/articleshow/132921898.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-05T17:41:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132925726,imgsize-950568.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Row erupts as UK Conservatives allow man jailed for antisemitic abuse to contest local election]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132929526.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/row-erupts-as-uk-conservatives-allow-man-jailed-for-antisemitic-abuse-to-contest-local-election/articleshow/132929526.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/row-erupts-as-uk-conservatives-allow-man-jailed-for-antisemitic-abuse-to-contest-local-election/articleshow/132929526.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-05T18:43:23+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132929526,imgsize-52213.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['They told you twice they don't want you': Andy Burnham reveals wife's reaction to PM bid]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132924199.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/they-told-you-twice-they-dont-want-you-andy-burnham-reveals-wifes-reaction-to-pm-bid/articleshow/132924199.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/they-told-you-twice-they-dont-want-you-andy-burnham-reveals-wifes-reaction-to-pm-bid/articleshow/132924199.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-05T17:35:15+05:30</p